barracks turns a pile of agent skills scattered across git repos into named,
versioned units you can deploy on demand.

Train a loadout, equip it with skill sources, then spawn it into whatever repo
you are working in - permanently, until a deadline, or only for as long as one
command runs. Recall it and the repo is exactly as you found it.

  barracks train frontend
  barracks equip frontend gh:owner/skills#main:skills --only 'react-*'
  barracks spawn frontend
  barracks run frontend -- claude

Skills are fetched once into a shared store and spawned as symlinks, so every
repo on your machine shares one copy. Nothing barracks did not create is ever
removed, and spawning leaves git status clean.

For a team repository, garrison a loadout instead: real files plus a committed
barracks.lock, so everyone who clones gets the identical skills at the identical
versions with no barracks installed.

  barracks garrison frontend
  barracks inspect

Usage:
  barracks [command]

Available Commands:
  assign      Set which agents a loadout installs into
  deployed    Show what is currently deployed here, spawned or committed
  disband     Delete a loadout definition
  equip       Equip a loadout with a git skill source
  garrison    Commit a loadout into this repository for the whole team
  help        Help about any command
  inspect     Check this checkout against barracks.lock
  list        List every loadout in the barracks
  recall      Recall a spawned loadout from the current repo
  rename      Rename a loadout, keeping everything it is deployed into working
  run         Spawn a loadout, run a command, recall on exit
  spawn       Spawn a loadout into the current repo
  strip       Detach an equipped source and take its skills back out
  targets     List the agents barracks can deploy to
  train       Train a new loadout
  tui         Open the full-screen roster
  upgrade     Re-resolve loadout sources and relink live spawns

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for barracks
  -q, --quiet     suppress the progress indicator and the flavor line (see also BARRACKS_QUIET)
  -v, --version   version for barracks

Use "barracks [command] --help" for more information about a command.
